@* The one place recovery codes are ever shown (issue #20). Rendered only in the response to the POST
   that created them - never from a redirect target, a query string, TempData or a cookie - and
   Relio does not store them in a retrievable form for display, so a refresh does not show them again.
   Authenticated responses already carry Cache-Control: no-store (Program.cs). *@

<MudText Typo="Typo.h3" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mb-2">Save your recovery codes</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mud-text-secondary mb-4">
    If you lose your phone, a recovery code lets you sign in instead of a code from the app. Each one
    works once. Keep them somewhere safe, like a password manager. Relio won't show them again.
</MudText>

<ol class="rl-recovery-codes" data-testid="recovery-codes">
    @foreach (var recoveryCode in Codes)
    {
        <li data-testid="recovery-code">@recoveryCode</li>
    }
</ol>

@code {
    /// <summary>The freshly issued codes, in the form Identity created them (<c>XXXXX-XXXXX</c>).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Codes { get; set; } = [];
}
